{
  "_": "The standup's dates read (docs/modules/solitaire-agile.md, \"What moved, and the window\"): ONE gh api graphql call per repo (per 50 aliases), the owner and name as variables. `query` is the text both halves send for its hashes and numbers, line for line (dates_query / Get-P20StandupDatesQuery): c<i> is the i-th hash's commit by object(expression:), i<n> issue n's labelled and assigned events. Each case is the parse of one answer's `repository` object (dates_from_answer / ConvertFrom-P20StandupDates): a commit is dated by its authoredDate only when GitHub resolved the hash to a commit whose oid begins with it -- an abbreviated hash resolves, a missing or ambiguous one answers null and is null here, never a guess; an issue's start is the earliest of a worker label being added and the issue being assigned, a label that routes to no worker is not a start, and an issue with no start is not a key of issueStarts. The same call reads co-author trailers (docs/hub/cards.md, \"How a card's agent is worked out\"): `trailerQuery` adds t<i>, the i-th trailer hash's commit with its oid, authoredDate and message, after the c and i aliases -- and with no trailer hashes the text is `query`'s, unchanged. A case's `trailers` are parsed into `messages` (a resolved trailer hash's first seven characters, lower case -> its message: an unknown hash's null object, or an oid that is not the hash, is skipped) and date their commit when it has no date yet; a case with no `messages` expects none. Asserted from tkTestToolkit -Rituals and Tests/test_rituals.py.",
